    "DISCOVER": {
      "Does the unterminated final segment count as a line for the longest-line measure? For 'a b c' with no terminator, should it report 3 or 0?": "Include it \u2014 report 3. The unterminated final segment DOES count as a line for the longest-line measure, even though the existing `lines` counter excludes it. So `a b c` with no terminator reports longest_line_words: 3.",
      "Should the output report only the word count of the longest line, or also its line number or text?": "Word count only. Report a single numeric field; no line number, no line text.",
      "What exact label should the new field use, and should it follow `lines: <L>` at the end of the output line?": "Use the label `longest_line_words: N` and place it at the end, after `lines: <L>`. Output becomes `words: W characters: C lines: L longest_line_words: N`."
    }
